WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.768
-You guys, we have been so happy

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:04.337
to have Fred Armisen
with us all week.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.339
Fred, how are you, my friend?
-I'm doing great.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.207
-It's so exciting
to have you here for a week

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:09.542
and this is really
exciting, too --

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.611
it is Opening Day
in Major League Baseball.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.879
I know you're a huge sports fan,

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:15.314
a huge baseball fan, huge.
-Huge, huge. Baseball.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:16.982
[ Laughter ]
-Which team do you think
has the best chances?

00:00:16.982 --> 00:00:18.484
-Phillies.
-Great.

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:20.587
[ Cheering and applause ]
Phillies all the way.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.755
-Phillies everywhere.
But I also heard --

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:24.691
is this true --
that you are launching,

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:28.627
next week is the opening day
of your rival baseball league?

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:30.463
-Yes.
-That's so exciting.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.365
-So I have this baseball league
that is like

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:36.902
it's players from every team...

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:39.838
-Uh-huh.
-...in both leagues,

00:00:39.838 --> 00:00:41.908
National and American.
-Great.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.443
You do know a lot
about baseball.
-I do.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.476
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.476 --> 00:00:45.945
But it's less about like,

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.180
"I'm from this team
or that team."

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.915
It's more like a crowd
of players on the field.

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:51.250
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.
-Right?

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.586
And it's more like
let's have fun.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.188
Let's throw a bunch
of baseballs around.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.790
[ Laughter ]
Like it doesn't have to be
so many rules.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.058
That's like from another time.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:01.727
Let's all just enjoy
this moment.

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:02.929
-Okay.
-So --

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.396
-So it's just a bunch of guys
on the field,

00:01:04.396 --> 00:01:06.332
throwing balls around?

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.334
-Yeah, but in a way
that's like sort of, you know,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.836
with enjoyment.
-Do --

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.105
[ Laughter ]
Is there a way to keep score?

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.840
-Yeah. So, so,
for every three times

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.110
that someone catches a ball,
right,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.078
that's 7 points.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:21.881
[ Laughter ]
Every fourth time, zero points.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.917
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.485
Any fastball that goes
to left field,

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.621
where four people catch those,

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.624
10 points, with 5 subtracted,
if it's from the opposing team.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.459
[ Laughter ]
-And that's it.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.562
-Those are the only rules?
-Those are the only rules.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:36.963
-Wait, how long
does the game take?

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.230
-Five minutes.
-Okay.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:38.898
-Quickly, yeah.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:42.935
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:44.737
-And what is it called,
if we're looking for it?

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.505
-It's just called
regular baseball.

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:47.807
[ Laughter ]
-Okay, great.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.608
-Give it up one more time
for Fred Armisen, everybody.

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:50.944
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Thank you.

